# penelope, the pattern editor of ipl_gprogs, built on the library's vidgets: set a cell and a dragged diagonal with the left button, clear a cell
# with the right, shift the tile with a transformation button, turn one symmetry on and set a mirrored pair, copy the tile into the list (tile
# menu), show the tile instead of the pattern (view menu), give the tile a note through a dialog (note menu), read its information box (meta i),
# save the list under a typed name (file menu, save as), quit (file menu). Cell j i of the 8 by 8 grid stands at 160+21j 70+21i.
click 1 170 80
wait
drag 1 170 80 317 227
wait
click 3 233 143
wait
# the first transformation button, shift up
click 1 56 71
wait
# the last symmetry button, then one cell: it and its mirror are set
click 1 216 392
wait
click 1 191 185
wait
# the tile menu held open, then its item copy
move 55 11
press 1
wait
move 60 136
release 1
wait
# the view menu, item tile
move 128 11
press 1
wait
move 130 46
release 1
wait
# the note menu, item edit: a dialog takes the note
move 163 11
press 1
wait
move 165 31
release 1
wait
# a dialog stands in the middle of the window and takes keys only with the pointer inside it
move 365 210
type w7
key Return
wait
# meta i: the information box, closed with Return
keydown Alt_L
key i
keyup Alt_L
wait
key Return
wait
# the file menu, item save as: a dialog takes the file name
move 18 11
press 1
wait
move 20 61
release 1
wait
move 365 210
type t.tle
key Return
wait
# the file menu, item quit
move 18 11
press 1
wait
move 20 106
release 1
